<BaseLayout title="Unexploded ordnance information" description="A growing public-interest resource on unexploded ordnance, its impacts, and professional clearance.">
  <section class="hero"><div class="container hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Field information / public awareness</p><h1>The war ended. The ordnance didn’t.</h1><p class="lead">Unexploded ordnance can remain dangerous long after a conflict has passed. UXO.ECO is building a clearer, source-led way to understand its lasting humanitarian and environmental consequences.</p><a class="action-link" href="/what-is-uxo">Start with the basics</a></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Why this exists</p><h2>Knowledge is part of safer ground.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>UXO can affect where people live, farm, rebuild, travel, and recover. Its consequences are not limited to the moment a weapon fails to detonate.</p><p>Our aim is straightforward: make dependable information easier to find, easier to understand, and more useful to people who want to learn, teach, report, or contribute responsibly.</p><a class="action-link" href="/impacts">Explore the impacts</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section section--deep"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Safety first</p><h2>Information is not clearance.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>Suspected explosive ordnance must be left alone and reported to the relevant local authorities or specialist services. UXO.ECO does not provide handling, removal, or disposal instructions.</p><p>Clearance is specialist work: planned, assessed, and carried out by qualified teams under applicable standards and local authority.</p><a class="action-link" href="/clearance">How professional clearance works</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section section--quiet"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">The long view</p><h2>Our goal is obsolescence.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>We want a world free from the threat posed by UXO and other explosive remnants of war. That means rigorous, professional work—not a promise that every object everywhere can be known with absolute certainty.</p><p>We hope UXO.ECO eventually becomes an archive of a problem people no longer need to navigate. Until then, it exists to point people toward dependable information and qualified help.</p><p><a href="https://whytrashearth.org" rel="noopener noreferrer">UXO.ECO is a WhyTrashEarth project.</a></p><a class="action-link" href="/mission">Read the mission &amp; end state</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
